WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:02.480
Hatice Cengiz, welcome to
Scandinavia.

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:13.820
I should say that this is the first time you talk
about this in English in an interview.

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:15.940
I'm very grateful for that.

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:18.800
We'll try.

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:21.620
Thank you for having me.

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:26.940
Both you and Jamal were experts on the
Middle East region.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:27.840
Yes.

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:30.740
So you didn't only have

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:34.360
a romantic relationship, you also had
an intellectual relationship, right?

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:36.240
Yes, of course.

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:42.360
He was a really, really, really
good voice for me to understand ...

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:51.100
I really liked Jamal before I met him, as a
writer, as a thinker, as a person.

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:51.880
So ...

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:55.260
But then you met him and things happened.

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:56.800
Yes.

00:00:56.980 --> 00:00:59.420
Apart from your conversations ...

00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:02.680
What is it
that you miss the most about Jamal?

00:01:03.220 --> 00:01:05.740
His voice.

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:14.500
And of course I miss a lot of
things, but it's not easy to talk about everything here.

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:21.040
We talked in the morning every day and I miss

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:28.440
his face. He was a really cute person.

00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:39.380
He was more than a husband, a lover and
boyfriend, he was like my my father and

00:01:39.380 --> 00:01:48.780
my brother and my mother sometimes. He was my advisor and teacher and best friend.

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:53.200
And I loved him a lot.

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:54.780
So ...

00:01:55.540 --> 00:02:00.480
And he was asking, when he visited Turkey, Istanbul,

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:05.780
asking about the best restaurants in Istanbul and

00:02:05.780 --> 00:02:10.400
took me to eat the best meal and ...

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:15.700
Do you still have his voice present in your head?

00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:18.040
Yes, of course.

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:21.720
His voice, you know ...

00:02:23.060 --> 00:02:27.200
Everyone knows now that they killed Jamal, but

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:31.140
I think Jamal's voice is everywhere.

00:02:31.940 --> 00:02:33.080
Like now.

00:02:33.660 --> 00:02:35.840
In Skavlan show in Sweden.

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:39.960
My voice is Jamal's voice.

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:44.340
I try to keep the story alive.

00:02:44.440 --> 00:02:48.540
It's kind of a horror
story, but it's about real people and

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:49.920
It really happened.

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:51.640
I know it's hard for
you to talk about.

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:54.680
You were supposed to marry.

00:02:55.060 --> 00:02:56.060
Yes.

00:02:56.060 --> 00:02:58.580
But before that, he had to go to the consulate.

00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:01.420
To the Saudi consulate in Istanbul.

00:03:01.460 --> 00:03:05.020
Because he needed some documents to be able to marry you.

00:03:05.020 --> 00:03:06.800
He entered and he didn't come back.

00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:08.280
What did he say to you before he went in?

00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:12.240
He told me: «see you soon».

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:14.600
«Wait for me here, I'll see you soon.»

00:03:14.680 --> 00:03:20.280
You thought it would go quite quite fast and
then you were standing there waiting for him ...

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:21.500
Yes.

00:03:21.960 --> 00:03:24.460
When did you start to worry?

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:29.220
After two hours, I think.

00:03:29.460 --> 00:03:32.020
No, after three hours maybe.

00:03:32.600 --> 00:03:40.120
I didn't think that something would happen inside the consulate.

00:03:40.340 --> 00:03:45.560
As a writer, as a Saudi
citizen, as a really really big journalist,

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:49.760
I didn't think about this.

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:54.300
I was trusting Jamal's opinion.

00:03:54.640 --> 00:03:56.600
He was relaxed, so you were relaxed, in a way?

00:03:56.660 --> 00:03:57.720
Yes, that's it.

00:03:58.020 --> 00:04:03.840
And you know, it was really
important for Jamal and for me at the same time

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:09.640
that we had to get this paper, and we thought it would be worth it to wait there.

00:04:10.580 --> 00:04:17.760
Did you ask the guards after,
I mean, did you talk to anyone?

00:04:18.620 --> 00:04:20.420
As time passed?

00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:24.800
I was really, really, really afraid. And then I called the consulate.

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:30.860
They said: «wait there, I'm coming».

00:04:30.860 --> 00:04:35.440
One came from inside, a Saudi person.

00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:39.080
And I told him that I'm Jamal's fiancée.

00:04:39.080 --> 00:04:41.640
And he was shocked.

00:04:41.800 --> 00:04:46.020
From his face, I understood

00:04:46.020 --> 00:04:48.980
that something had happened.

00:04:50.020 --> 00:04:55.320
And then I urgently

00:04:56.940 --> 00:04:59.240
called my best friend

00:04:59.540 --> 00:05:04.440
and I told her: «come here
very very quickly».

00:05:04.960 --> 00:05:10.580
And then I called someone who is responsible at the government.

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:13.260
And then one-two-three other calls.

00:05:13.260 --> 00:05:17.460
When did you realize that he probably
wasn't alive anymore?

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:22.900
You know, if you remember the 19th of October announcement ....

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:26.860
The Saudi announcement on the 19th of October.

00:05:26.860 --> 00:05:31.640
They said that Jamal was killed inside the consulate.

00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:36.060
I was expecting

00:05:36.460 --> 00:05:38.700
something different because ...

00:05:38.860 --> 00:05:41.860
I didn't believe it because ...

00:05:42.720 --> 00:05:48.880
It's really stupid to kill Jamal inside the consulate.

00:05:49.040 --> 00:05:54.060
It's not acceptable, it's not a normal thing.

00:05:54.300 --> 00:06:01.880
So you kept kept the hope and the faith

00:06:01.880 --> 00:06:04.740
that he was alive for days and weeks?

00:06:04.740 --> 00:06:08.120
Because, you know, Jamal told me

00:06:08.340 --> 00:06:18.120
often that «my country is really, really beautiful and
good and you will change your opinion of my country».

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:24.640
As you know, I'm a
researcher and I had some idea about

00:06:24.640 --> 00:06:28.320
Saudi Arabia, but it wasn't all good.

00:06:28.880 --> 00:06:30.580
And he was saying to me:

00:06:30.580 --> 00:06:36.440
«I will change your opinion with time and you will

00:06:36.960 --> 00:06:44.040
become a very professional writer about my country
because of me.

00:06:44.080 --> 00:06:47.940
I will teach you a lot of things». And then

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:51.780
he was really
optimistic.

00:06:51.980 --> 00:06:55.460
So I tried to remember these points.

00:06:55.780 --> 00:06:57.460
So ...

00:06:58.240 --> 00:07:02.640
«No, no, no, it's so huge, someone
killed Jamal inside to consulate?»

00:07:02.780 --> 00:07:06.940
But five men have recently been
sentenced to death.

00:07:07.300 --> 00:07:08.200
Yes.

00:07:08.200 --> 00:07:09.860
For this crime in Saudi Arabia.

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:12.380
What are your thoughts on that?

00:07:14.480 --> 00:07:20.000
You know, it's really like a
joke to me.

00:07:20.180 --> 00:07:22.000
It's unacceptable, really.

00:07:22.180 --> 00:07:27.140
Because we don't know any details about
this investigation.

00:07:27.260 --> 00:07:31.360
They only told us about five men who were not named.

00:07:31.640 --> 00:07:34.440
And why are they five?

00:07:34.440 --> 00:07:39.260
Because more than ten people came to Turkey!

00:07:39.260 --> 00:07:43.740
And we want real punishment.

00:07:43.740 --> 00:07:45.420
Even for the ones who ordered it.

00:07:45.440 --> 00:07:47.720
According to CIA and the UN,

00:07:47.920 --> 00:07:54.260
it's also possible that the crown
prince himself has been involved in some way.

00:07:54.280 --> 00:07:56.920
Although he denies this firmly.

00:07:57.840 --> 00:07:59.580
What do you think?

00:07:59.600 --> 00:08:03.180
As you know, a special rapporteur in the UN,

00:08:03.780 --> 00:08:07.860
said that there's a very, very big ...

00:08:11.880 --> 00:08:14.180
I forgot the word.

00:08:14.680 --> 00:08:16.040
Possibility!

00:08:16.180 --> 00:08:24.200
... possibility that some people from the high level were involved this crime.

00:08:25.480 --> 00:08:37.560
So that's why are requesting an international
investigation to get justice for Jamal and the others.

00:08:37.820 --> 00:08:45.380
The fact that many
countries, among them I think Norway and Sweden,

00:08:45.520 --> 00:08:51.560
have done nothing, really, does that
disappoint you?

00:08:51.760 --> 00:08:54.020
It's really, really disappointing.

00:08:54.960 --> 00:08:59.640
As you know, it's a really big shame for all people

00:08:59.820 --> 00:09:02.640
around the world, not only Swedish people.

00:09:02.660 --> 00:09:08.720
And that's because they try to normalize

00:09:08.720 --> 00:09:12.600
their relationship with Saudi Arabia.

00:09:12.760 --> 00:09:16.500
What's the difference between Sweden and Saudi
Arabia in this case?

00:09:17.020 --> 00:09:18.200
Tell me!

00:09:18.220 --> 00:09:20.220
You tried to cover this crime.

00:09:20.600 --> 00:09:22.100
What's the difference between them?

00:09:22.180 --> 00:09:23.440
There's nothing.

00:09:23.440 --> 00:09:25.780
I wonder, the day

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:30.000
that started as a normal day for
you and Jamal ...

00:09:32.220 --> 00:09:37.220
It was quite a normal day, you were supposed to
go to the consulate to get this paper,

00:09:37.220 --> 00:09:39.960
what were the plans for the day
afterwards?

00:09:41.520 --> 00:09:42.980
The plan was ...

00:09:45.420 --> 00:09:53.740
We had already bought some things for our flat, even a refrigerator and a washing machine.

00:09:54.060 --> 00:10:00.460
I was waiting for this
stuff and I called them and asked about ...

00:10:00.640 --> 00:10:09.320
If we could come today and change some things. And buy things to our house.

00:10:09.440 --> 00:10:12.200
And then dinner with our friends.

00:10:12.680 --> 00:10:15.540
It was a really full day for us.

00:10:15.620 --> 00:10:16.980
So that was the plan?

00:10:16.980 --> 00:10:18.460
Yes, that was the plan.

00:10:18.780 --> 00:10:24.120
If you were able
to ask him a question now, what would that be?

00:10:25.700 --> 00:10:30.100
I blamed myself a lot.

00:10:30.500 --> 00:10:33.140
I was thinking ...

00:10:33.340 --> 00:10:41.700
Why weren't we more careful?

00:10:41.700 --> 00:10:44.300
You blamed yourself because ..?

00:10:44.740 --> 00:10:46.520
Because why ...

00:10:47.860 --> 00:10:51.240
I don't know why I blamed myself, but ...

00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:54.780
You know, I had to say something.

00:10:54.780 --> 00:10:58.940
I had to say something to myself.

00:11:01.020 --> 00:11:02.440
Maybe ...

00:11:02.440 --> 00:11:05.160
It's a very difficult question.

00:11:05.160 --> 00:11:07.900
What would I ask Jamal?

00:11:10.240 --> 00:11:13.640
Why, Jamal,

00:11:14.380 --> 00:11:17.760
do you have such an optimistic

00:11:18.820 --> 00:11:21.600
opinion of your country,

00:11:21.780 --> 00:11:25.100
more than they deserve?

00:11:26.040 --> 00:11:27.720
Because they killed you.

00:11:27.940 --> 00:11:29.800
Can I ask one question?

00:11:30.020 --> 00:11:34.300
Has anybody from Saudi Arabia approached you after
this?

00:11:34.720 --> 00:11:36.020
No, no, no.

00:11:36.120 --> 00:11:37.600
No one called me.

00:11:37.680 --> 00:11:42.480
Why would they call me? About what? What would they say?

00:11:43.300 --> 00:11:45.160
Sorry, or something like that?

00:11:45.880 --> 00:11:48.140
A «sorry» would not be for me, it would be for everyone.

00:11:48.320 --> 00:11:51.840
And we need punishment, not apologies.

00:11:52.900 --> 00:11:55.940
Hatice, how do you see your life in five years?

00:11:56.140 --> 00:11:58.460
I'll be doing something for Jamal.

00:11:58.820 --> 00:12:00.920
To keep his name alive.

00:12:01.060 --> 00:12:03.920
And his case, and his story.

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:06.360
And his values, our values.

00:12:06.400 --> 00:12:12.460
So I think that's my first responsibility

00:12:12.480 --> 00:12:15.120
as a woman also.

00:12:15.680 --> 00:12:18.320
Hatice, thank you so much for being with us tonight.

00:12:18.440 --> 00:12:20.300
Thank you. Thank you.

